From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Ericson <John.Ericson@Obsidian.Systems>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 18:19:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] cmd/sgs/lorder: find nm on $PATH, and report errors on stderr

Two problems when running lorder outside a normal illumos install:

- It invoked `/usr/bin/nm` by absolute path. Look nm up on `$PATH` instead,
  and let `$NM` override it, which is what a cross-build needs in order to
  point at the target's nm.

- Its usage and "cannot open" messages went to stdout. lorder's stdout is
  consumed by a pipeline -- libc builds its archive with
  `ar q $@ \`lorder ... | tsort\`` -- so an error message got spliced into
  the object list and passed to ar as filenames:

      ar: cannot: No such file or directory

  Diagnostics belong on stderr.

Assisted-by: Claude Code (Claude Opus 5)
---
 usr/src/cmd/sgs/lorder/lorder.sh | 9 ++++-----
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/usr/src/cmd/sgs/lorder/lorder.sh b/usr/src/cmd/sgs/lorder/lorder.sh
index 152d9ba9ea..0b6b1c8b51 100644
--- a/usr/src/cmd/sgs/lorder/lorder.sh
+++ b/usr/src/cmd/sgs/lorder/lorder.sh
@@ -36,25 +36,24 @@ else
 fi
 trap "rm -f $TDIR/$$symdef $TDIR/$$symref $TDIR/$$tmp; exit"  1 2 13 15
 PFX=
-WHERE=/usr/bin
 
 USAGE="Usage: ${PFX}lorder file ..."
 for i in "$@"
 do
 	case "$i" in
-	-*)	echo "$USAGE";
+	-*)	echo "$USAGE" >&2;
 		exit 2;;
 	esac
 
 	if [ ! -r "$i" ]
 	then
-		echo "${PFX}lorder: $i: cannot open"
+		echo "${PFX}lorder: $i: cannot open" >&2
 		exit 2;
 	fi
 done
 
 case $# in
-0)	echo "$USAGE"
+0)	echo "$USAGE" >&2
 	exit 2;;
 1)	case $1 in
 	*.o)	set $1 $1
@@ -85,7 +84,7 @@ esac
 #	symbol referenced (symref) file.
 #
 #
-${WHERE}/${PFX}nm -p $* 2>$TDIR/$$tmp | sed -e '/^[ 	]*$/d' -e '
+${NM:-${PFX}nm} -p $* 2>$TDIR/$$tmp | sed -e '/^[ 	]*$/d' -e '
 	/^[0-9]* R $/d
 	/ [[:lower:]FLS] /d
 	/[^]]:$/{
